{"case_id":"C011","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","configuration","input_semantics"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":86,"affected_functions":["OptimiserSettings::removeInvalidCharacters","LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput","OptimiserSuite::runSequence"],"reason":"S1 adds the public string-processing entry point OptimiserSettings::removeInvalidCharacters, but H0 never invokes it or supplies independently controlled optimizer-sequence text. H0 derives settings solely through randomYulOptimiserSequence(_size), limiting optimizer configuration to permutations of DefaultYulOptimiserSteps selected by the 0–600 input size. Consequently it cannot exercise removeInvalidCharacters on arbitrary bytes or deliberately target the changed unknown-abbreviation path in OptimiserSuite::runSequence. This uncovered API and its input semantics did not exist in S0, so the material gap is commit-induced.","evidence":["S1 newly defines OptimiserSettings::removeInvalidCharacters(const std::string& _input), which filters caller-controlled text using validCharacters.","H0 constructs optSequence only with OptimiserSettings::randomYulOptimiserSequence(_size) and passes it to OptimiserSettings::fuzz(optSequence); it never calls removeInvalidCharacters.","H0 rejects _size values above 600, so optimizer-sequence selection through _size has at most 601 seed values and is not byte-for-byte controlled by the fuzz input.","OptimiserSuite::runSequence changes abbreviationsToSteps to catch std::out_of_range for an abbreviation, while H0's sequence characters originate from DefaultYulOptimiserSteps rather than independently supplied sequence text.","The AsmAnalyzer::analyzeStrictAssertCorrect change only prints AsmPrinter output and does not itself require additional harness state or input control."],"recommended_action":"Extend H0 so a bounded portion of the fuzz bytes controls optimizer-sequence text, pass it through OptimiserSettings::removeInvalidCharacters, and use the